---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES Lore | XRP KIDs Canon, FRET, Alpha Aaron and Block Buster OG"
  description="Internal canon hub for NO BALL GAMES lore including XRP KIDs (100/89/11), Alpha Aaron, FRET, $PMSL and the 2035 New Dawn sign-as-door arc."
  current="lore"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Lore archive</span>
    <h1>Internal canon of the NO BALL GAMES universe.</h1>
    <p>
      This page presents the XRP KIDs branch as internal canon/lore, not verified real-world history. Technical chain claims still require issuer and ledger proof before being treated as factual.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Canon timeline spine</h2>
      <p>Key internal events from genesis through New Dawn.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2025</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>100 genesis XRP KIDs</h3>
          <p>The collection starts as a 100-piece genesis set tied to NO BALL GAMES rebellion energy.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2028–2029</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Alpha Aaron capture arc</h3>
          <p>Canon states Alpha Aaron seizes 89 of the 100 KIDs, shifting the world from collection culture into control conflict.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2029+</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>11 free + FRET response</h3>
          <p>The remaining 11 free KIDs become the resistance core. FRET (Fresh Rapid Elite Team) forms as a street-level network around the Barbican.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Fork phase</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>$PMSL hard-fork shield</h3>
          <p>$PMSL appears in canon as a protective fork layer around the free KIDs during the anti-capture phase.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Fibonacci era</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Block Buster OG reveal</h3>
          <p>The hidden Block Buster OG 1/1 is revealed as a memory/archive intervention layer connected to Charlie Buster.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2035</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>New Dawn: signs become doors</h3>
          <p>Canon closes with the sign no longer acting as a warning but as a route marker, portal and survival logic for the remaining free KIDs.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Canon cards</h2>
      <p>Main characters, factions and systems.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">XRP KIDs</span>
        <h3>100 / 89 / 11 structure</h3>
        <p>100 genesis KIDs, 89 captured, 11 free. These counts are internal canon anchors for narrative pages.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Alpha Aaron</span>
        <h3>Machine capture force</h3>
        <p>Antagonist symbol of extraction and algorithmic control trying to own culture rather than understand it.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">FRET</span>
        <h3>Fresh Rapid Elite Team</h3>
        <p>Grassroots resistance unit of artists, coders, collectors and signal runners operating through urban back routes.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">$PMSL</span>
        <h3>Humour-coded fork shield</h3>
        <p>Lore token shield for the 11 free KIDs. Public token specifics must remain source-needed until proven.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Block Buster OG</span>
        <h3>Hidden archive intervention</h3>
        <p>Mythic 1/1 survival layer carrying memory, timing and anti-control logic into the late timeline.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Lore discipline</span>
      <h2>Canon is not automatic proof.</h2>
      <p>
        Keep all lore events labelled as internal canon. Any issuer addresses, wallet records, token data or marketplace history must be verified before publication as real-world fact.
      </p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}research/`}>Review truth baseline →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Next read</span>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li><a class="inline-link" href={`${base}xrp/`}>XRP hub timeline and claim guardrails</a></li>
        <li><a class="inline-link" href={`${base}community/`}>Community participation and FRET framing</a></li>
        <li><a class="inline-link" href={`${base}collections/`}>Collector lanes across physical and digital</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
